# Responsibilities
  text: Learn, develop, maintain, and enhance automated test scripts under the guidance of more senior automation team members.
  text: Participate in the creation and execution of test cases, test plans, and test scenarios based on business requirements.
  text: Demonstrate flexibility in shifting between manual validation and automation work depending on delivery timelines, feature complexity, and t
  text: Continuously build technical testing knowledge, including exposure to automation frameworks, scripting, CI/CD, and quality engineering best 
  text: Communicate effectively in a remote environment, including maintaining an active on-camera presence during meetings when expected.
# Qualifications
  text: Basic understanding of the software development lifecycle (SDLC) and/or Agile delivery practices.
  text: Familiarity with test automation concepts and an interest in building skills in automation tools and frameworks.
  text: Exposure to one or more programming or scripting languages such as JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, Python, or C#.
  text: Strong communication skills and the ability to work effectively with cross-functional teams.
  text: Health IT experience (a plus)
